-- DuplicateInterfaceMethod (Q1, Stage B / Phase 4b): two `interface`s declared in
-- ONE module declare the same METHOD name `n`.
--
-- ⭐ THERE IS NO OCCURRENCE OF `n` ANYWHERE IN THIS FILE, ON PURPOSE. The rule is on
-- the DECLARATION, not on an ambiguous use, so a file that merely declares the
-- collision and never exercises it must still be rejected. A fixture that called `n`
-- would pass under either rule and could not tell them apart.
--
-- ⚠️ THIS SHAPE COMPILED BEFORE. With impls at disjoint receivers it ran correctly
-- (it was test/iface_order_fixtures/control-shared-method-name-disjoint-receivers/).
-- The narrowing is the owner ruling, not an accident — see ifaceMethodCollisions in
-- compiler/frontend/resolve.mdk.
interface E1 a where
  n : a -> Int

interface E2 a where
  n : a -> Int

main = println 0
